{
  "description": "Key matching through hit() (Format 7.2, 10.1, 11.4, 11.5): whole words, so no letter, mark or number (Unicode L, M, N) right before or after a match; case compared by Unicode simple case folding; keys in Han, Hiragana and the other listed scripts match anywhere; regex keys, with every line break in the scanned text written as \\n; the speaker's name; knowledge, hidden messages and scanDepth decide what is scanned",
  "note": "Each root is its own path, so each test scans one message unless it says otherwise. r4 writes café as e followed by U+0301. In r6, Ί (U+038A) folds to ί (U+03AF) and Σ and ς both fold to σ; ß and İ have no simple folding. r13 separates a and b with CRLF, and r14 with U+2028, so /^b/m matches in both; /a.b/s matches r13 only because its CRLF is one \\n.",
  "bundle": {
    "kind": "bundle",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "name": "Ann",
        "description": "Ann."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "name": "Bea",
        "description": "Bea."
      }
    ],
    "scenarios": [
      {
        "id": "s",
        "cast": [
          {},
          {
            "character": "a"
          },
          {
            "character": "b"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
